          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            generalize from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-categories
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F : K \to
                    C
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              (a morphism of the underlying
              = succeed "s)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %strong limit
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is, if it exists, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+a+quasi-category"} quasi-categorical terminal object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over quasi-category
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{/F}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi TerminalObj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F \coloneqq TerminalObj(C_{/F})
            %p (well defined up to a contractible space of choices).
            %p
              A
              %strong colimit
              in a quasi-category is accordingly a limit in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+quasi-category"} opposite quasi-category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Notice from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+quasi-categories"} join of quasi-categories
              that there are two definitions – denoted
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamondsuit
              – of join, which yield results that differ as simplicial sets, though are equivalent as quasi-categories.
            %p
              The notation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{/F}
              denotes the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over quasi-category
              induced from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{/F}
              denotes that induced from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamondsuit
            %p So we also have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi TerminalObj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F \coloneqq TerminalObj(C^{/F})
                    \\,.
            %p
              See
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 4.2.1.5
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#InTermsOfSlices
            In terms of slice
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon K \to \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              with
              = succeed "-colimiting" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⋆
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f \colon K \star \Delta^0 \to \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} slice quasi-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\tilde f} \to \mathcal{C}_{f}
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+Kan+fibration"} acyclic Kan fibration
          #SlicingOverLimitingCone.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{K} \to \mathcal{C}
              a diagram in an
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F
              its limit, there is a natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/F} \simeq \mathcal{C}_{/\underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F}
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} slice (∞,1)-categories
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              (the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              over
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ←
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim}F
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F \colon \Delta^0 \star \mathcal{K} \to \mathcal{C}
              be the limiting cone. The canonical cospan of
              = succeed "-functors" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo ←
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast \to \Delta^0 \star \mathcal{K} \leftarrow \mathcal{K}
            %p
              induces a span of slice
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                        %mi F
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mover
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\underset{\leftarrow}{\lim}F}
                    \\leftarrow
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\tilde F}
                    \\rightarrow
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/F}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The right functor is an equivalence by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SlicingOverLimitingCone"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} final (∞,1)-functor
              (by the Examples discussed there) and hence is an equivalence by the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} slice (∞,1)-category
              (
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 4.1.1.8
              ).
          %p
            This appears for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, proof of prop. 1.2.13.8
            ).
          %h3#in_terms_of_hom_adjunction
            In terms of
            = succeed "-Hom" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The definition of the limit in a quasi-category in terms of terminal objects in the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over quasi-category
            is well adapted to the particular nature the incarnation of
            = succeed "-categories" do
