          #InfinityGroupoidalCoLimitsViaIntegrationAndSlicing.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p Let the assumptions be as above. Then:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  = succeed "-colimit" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is equivalent to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_F
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mi F
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} F \simeq E_F
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  = succeed "-limit" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is equivalent to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+sections"} ∞-groupoid of sections
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_F \to X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim} \simeq \Gamma_X(E_F)
                        \\,.
          %p
            The statement for the colimit is corollary 3.3.4.6 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The form of the statement in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityGroupoidalCoLimitsViaIntegrationAndSlicing"}
              is the special case of the general form of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28co-%29limits"} internal (co-)limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} inftyGrpd
                      %mi small
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core(\inftyGrpd_{small})
              its small
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
              %em
                %a{:href => "internal+%28co-%29limit#ExamplesInfinityGroupoidal"} internal (co-)limit – Groupoidal homotopy (co-)limits
              for more on this.
          %h3#ColimitsInInfinityCat
            Limits and colimits with values in
            = succeed "Cat" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : D \to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              = succeed "-colimit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and then inverting the
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+morphism"} Cartesian morphism
            %p
              Formally this means, with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+Cartesian+fibrations"} model structure for Cartesian fibrations
              that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_\to F \simeq (\int F)^\sharp
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of the presentation of
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+sets"} marked simplicial sets
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, corollary 3.3.4.3
          %p
            For the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            takes values in ordinary categories see also at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/2-limit#2ColimitsInCat"} 2-limits in Cat
          %h3#limits_in_functor_categories
            Limits in
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            that admits small
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C)
            has all small limits and colimits, and these are computed objectwise. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+and+colimits+by+example"} limits and colimits by example
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-functors
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} colimits
              indexed by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              be a small quasi-category. Then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Func
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C)
                  has all
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  A morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi K
                          %mo ▹
                        %mo →
                        %mi Func
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\triangleright \to Func(D,C)
                  is a colimiting cocone precisely if for each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
                  the induced morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi K
                          %mo ▹
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\triangleright \to C
                  is a colimiting cocone.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, corollary 5.1.2.3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"}> limit
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+limit"} internal limit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  \-limit
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"}> finite (∞,1)-limit
                    ,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} relative (∞,1)-limit
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} lax (∞,1)-colimit
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The definition of limit in quasi-categories is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em Quasi-categories and Kan complexes
              Journal of Pure and Applied Algebra 175 (2002), 207-222.
          %p A brief survey is on page 159 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em The theory of quasicategories and its applications
              lectures at
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.cat/HigherCategories/hc2.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A detailed account is in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0608/0608040v4.pdf#page=48"} definition 1.2.13.4, p. 48
            in
          %ul#Lurie
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Do homotopy limits compute limits in the associated quasicategory in the non-combinatorial model category case?
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/176111/do-homotopy-limits-compute-limits-in-the-associated-quasicategory-in-the-non-com/176142#176142"} MO/176111/176142
          %p
            A discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              Martina Rovelli,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Weighted limits in an (∞,1)-category
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.00805"} arxiv:1902.00805
          %p A discussion of free colimit completion constructions is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              %em Free colimit completion in ∞-categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.08582"}> arXiv:2210.08582
              )
          %p
            Discussion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+internal+to+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} internal to
            any
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Martini"}> Louis Martini
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastian+Wolf"} Sebastian Wolf
              %em Limits and colimits in internal higher category theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.14495"}> arXiv:2111.14495
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            A formalization of some aspects of
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is
            = succeed "-coded" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillaume+Brunerie"}> Guillaume Brunerie
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/guillaumebrunerie/HoTT/tree/master/Coq/Limits"} HoTT/Coq/Limits
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy Colimits and a Descent Theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://video.ias.edu/univalent-1213-0314-EgbertRijke"} video
